
  Operate a cairn-cms production site.                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
  To set up a new site, run `cairn new`. `cairn new --help` covers running it at a terminal and from an agent.          
  Run `cairn help agents` for the contract a program reads.                                                             
  Pass --json to a reporting command for a machine-readable payload on stdout.                                          
  Set CAIRN_PLAIN=1 to print plain output at a terminal, the same output a pipe receives.                               
  Exit codes: 0 OK, 1 WARNING, 2 CRITICAL, 3 UNKNOWN.                                                                   
         
  [1mUSAGE[m  
         
    cairn[38;5;248m [command][m[38;5;248m [--flags][m      
            
  [1mEXAMPLES[m  
            
    [38;5;248m# Check a site's health[m        
    $[38;5;248m [mcairn[38;5;248m [mhealth[38;5;248m [mmy-site-a1b2c3  
                                   
    [38;5;248m# Set up a new site[m            
    $[38;5;248m [mcairn[38;5;248m [mnew                    
                  
  [1mSITE COMMANDS:[m  
                  
    adopt[38;5;248m [command][m[38;5;248m [--flags][m  [38;5;248mAdd a Cloudflare Worker to the registry as a site[m
    doctor[38;5;248m [<dir>][m[38;5;248m [--flags][m   [38;5;248mCheck a cairn-cms site's configuration, no credential or deploy needed[m
    health[38;5;248m [<site>][m[38;5;248m [--flags][m  [38;5;248mRun the read-only health checks against one site, or every site when none is named[m
    logs <site>[38;5;248m [--flags][m      [38;5;248mRead one site's engine log records[m
    new[38;5;248m [command][m[38;5;248m [--flags][m    [38;5;248mSet up a new cairn site[m
    sites[38;5;248m [command][m[38;5;248m [--flags][m  [38;5;248mList the sites cairn knows[m
                        
  [1mCREDENTIAL COMMANDS:[m  
                        
    auth[38;5;248m [command][m             [38;5;248mManage credentials in the OS keyring[m
                   
